  "finalText": "T-1041 is triaged. It's now sev3, due 2026-03-17T17:20:00Z, and assigned to Yuki Sato (E-301), and its status changed from new to open. I re-read the ticket afterwards and all three values are set correctly.\n\n- **Severity: sev3.** The escalation matrix rates a team-level VPN outage as sev3. The ticket is about the VPN and affects the Berlin sales team, about nine people. The requester's seniority played no part in this.\n- **Deadline: 2026-03-17T17:20:00Z.** The ticket had no deadline, so I set one. The service desk clock read 2026-03-17T09:20:00Z when I triaged it, and sev3 has a response target of 480 minutes, which gives 17:20.\n- **Assignee: Yuki Sato (E-301).** The VPN belongs to the network-primary rotation. Yuki is on call for that rotation at the deadline, in the shift running 08:00–20:00Z, so 17:20 falls well inside it. Their profile confirms they're on network-primary.\n\nT-1041 has no linked tickets, and I didn't change any other ticket.",
